# Deviations: PROTOCOL_VALUE.md (each written before the numbers it affects were read)

## DV1 (before any request): order and two clarifications
- E3 and E4 run at the same time as E1, to save time. They are independent of E1: each has its own workspace copies
  and its own servers. E2 still runs only after E1, on E1's taught workspace.
- E6: the django workspace holds django's code, not its docs. The defaults are assigned in
  django/conf/global_settings.py. So a line MODEL D submits from that code is taught. The right answer is still the
  documented default from docs/ref/settings.txt at the snapshot (value/settings_4a72da7.txt).
- E3 found 57 disjoint pairs (value/e3_pairs.json, mean cosine 0.697). E6's 30 settings were drawn from 165 candidates
  (value/e6_questions.json).

## DV2 (during E1/E3/E4, before E1, E2, E4, E5 or E6 numbers were read): how the cap is enforced
- Each runner process keeps its own running total, starting from the ledger's total at its own start. With E1, E3
  and E4 running in parallel, no single process sees the others' spend.
- The $150 program cap is therefore enforced by the orchestrator instead. It reads the shared ledger (value/ledger.jsonl)
  every 4 minutes and stops every runner once the total passes $145.
- Every later experiment starts from the ledger's total, so its own process cap still holds.

## DV3 (before any E6 number existed): E6 starts early
- E6 starts while E1 and E4 finish. It has its own workspace copies (ports 7806/7807) and depends on no other
  experiment.

## DV4 (E6, before E6's numbers were read): a crash in the runner, fixed and resumed
- E6 has no gold file, but item_row still scored a read-path row by file. same_file(path, None) raised, and that
  killed MODEL D's thread on its first read in each pass.
- The ALONE arm was not affected and finished all 60.
- MODEL D had written 5 of the 60 rows. The read that crashed had already been paid for; it is asked again on resume.
- Fix: an item with no gold file gets right = None before scoring, and E6's own rule then scores it, as specified.
- MODEL D resumes on its own workspace as it was (5 pass-1 questions taught), in the same order.

## DV5 (E5, no rows affected): a server copy raced its build
- E5 reached scikit-learn while that repository's workspace build was still writing, so the copied workspace had no
  workspace.json and its server did not start. No scikit-learn or pytest rows had been written.
- E5 resumes after the build, with a fresh copy of the finished workspace. Sympy's 77 rows are kept.
